# THEKRA BACKEND — CODE STANDARDS (NestJS · Prisma · PostgreSQL)

This folder (`backend/`) is opened as its own Cursor project root. Paths below are relative to `backend/` unless
they start with `docs/` (which lives one level up, at the monorepo root: `../docs/`).

## Source of Truth (READ BEFORE ANY TASK)

| Question | Authority |
| --- | --- |
| Which modules exist, which endpoints, request/response shapes, DTO fields, auth design, test cases, build order | `../docs/plan/backend-plan.md` |
| The data model (models, fields, relations, enums, unique constraints) | `../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` + `prisma/schema.prisma` |
| Ingestion, provider mappings, curation workflow, seed data | `../docs/plan/content-pipeline-plan.md` |
| Cross-cutting decisions (IDs like B5, D7) | `../docs/TECHNICAL_PLAN.md` → "Open decisions" table |

This file governs **HOW** code is written, never **WHAT** is built. If this file and `backend-plan.md` ever
disagree on a concrete decision (a path, a field, a status code, a module name), **`backend-plan.md` wins** —
follow it and tell the user about the conflict so this file can be corrected. Never "resolve" a conflict by
inventing a third option.

Before implementing an endpoint, open its entry in `backend-plan.md` §3 and implement exactly that contract:
path, auth column, query/body fields, response shape, status codes.

---

## Core Principles

- Clean, readable, maintainable code. DRY. KISS — the simplest solution that satisfies the plan.
- Small units: a service method does one thing; if a method passes ~50 lines, extract a private helper.
- Meaningful names; self-documenting code. Comments only for non-obvious decisions (e.g. *why* the grade
  filter is an `OR` clause), never to narrate what the next line does.
- Do NOT create `.md` files, `example-usage.ts`, scratch scripts, or demo files unless the user asks.
- Old logic that works is an asset: reuse or lightly extend it, don't write a "clean new" parallel version.

---

## ESM Discipline (MANDATORY — repo fact)

`package.json` has `"type": "module"` and `tsconfig.json` uses `"module": "nodenext"`. Therefore:

- Every **relative** import ends in `.js` (yes, `.js`, even though the file on disk is `.ts`). This is exactly
  how the scaffold already does it:

  ```ts
  // src/main.ts
  import { AppModule } from './app.module.js';

  // src/app.module.ts
  import { AppController } from './app.controller.js';
  import { AppService } from './app.service.js';
  ```

- Package imports stay bare (`'@nestjs/common'`, `'@prisma/client'`) — no extension.
- No `require()`, no `module.exports`, no `__dirname` (use `import.meta.dirname` if a path is truly needed),
  no extensionless relative imports. Top-level `await` is allowed (`main.ts` already uses it).
- Directory imports (`'./dto'`) do not resolve under `nodenext` — import the file (`'./dto/create-sin.dto.js'`).

---

## Module Boundaries (MANDATORY)

The approved module list is **exactly** `backend-plan.md` §1:

```
src/prisma/            PrismaModule (@Global) + PrismaService
src/common/            cross-cutting: dto/, interceptors/, filters/, pipes/, decorators/, text/, mappers/
src/health/            GET /health, GET /health/ready (unprefixed)
src/modules/quran/          src/modules/hadith/         src/modules/sins/
src/modules/good-deeds/     src/modules/classification/ src/modules/content-sync/
src/modules/quotes/         src/modules/sources/        src/modules/tags/
src/modules/auth/           src/modules/users/          src/modules/favorites/
```

- Before creating any new module folder, check this list. If the task seems to need a module that is not on
  it, **STOP and ask the user** — do not invent `modules/search`, `modules/admin`, `modules/shared`, etc.
  Admin routes live in `<name>.admin.controller.ts` inside the owning module, not in a separate admin module.
- Existing folder names must not be renamed (`quran`, `hadith`, `sins`, `good-deeds`, `classification`,
  `content-sync`).
- Per-module file convention (§1): `<name>.module.ts`, `<name>.controller.ts`, `<name>.admin.controller.ts`
  (only where admin routes exist), `<name>.service.ts`, `dto/`, `entities/`, `<name>.service.spec.ts`.
- Respect each module's **Owns (writes)** column in §1.2–§1.10. A module writes only the models it owns; to
  change another module's model, call that module's exported service.
- Import direction is one-way where the plan says so (e.g. `sins → good-deeds`, never back). If you reach for
  `forwardRef()`, the design is wrong — stop and re-read §1.
- `PrismaModule` is `@Global()`: do not re-import it in feature modules.
- Build order is §12. Do not build a module whose dependencies (e.g. `quotes/` before `sins/`) don't exist yet.

---

## Use What Already Exists First (MANDATORY)

Before writing ANY new DTO, service method, mapper, decorator, pipe, guard, or helper:

1. **Grep first.** Search `src/common/` and the relevant existing module(s) for the concept and likely names
   (`to*Dto`, `build*Include`, `*OrderBy`, `normalize*`, `Parse*Pipe`, `*.dto.ts`).
2. **Reuse > Extend > Create**, in that order. Create only when nothing fits; if something is ~80% similar,
   ask the user before writing a sibling.
3. **The quote projection exists exactly once.** `QuotesService.toQuoteDto(row, locale)`,
   `buildQuoteInclude(locale)` and `linkOrderBy()` (with the pure mapper in `common/mappers/quote.mapper.ts`)
   are the only way a `Quote` row becomes a `QuoteDto`. `sins`, `good-deeds`, `quran`, `hadith`, `tags` and
   `favorites` import and call them — they never hand-build a `QuoteDto`, never write their own `include` for
   a quote, never pick a translation themselves.
4. Shared request pieces live in `common/`: `PaginationQueryDto`, `LocaleQueryDto`, `@TransformToArray()`,
   `@CurrentUser()`, `@Roles()`, `@Public()`, `arabic-normalizer.ts`. Extend them (`extends PaginationQueryDto`),
   never copy their fields into a new DTO. `GoodDeedQuotesQueryDto` reuses `SinQuotesQueryDto` (§5.3).
5. When two helpers already do the same job, consolidate to one and point every caller at it.

**Anti-overengineering:** don't create a file for a single tiny export, don't add a `constants/` or `utils/`
folder for one value, don't add option bags/overloads/generics "for later". A constant used by one service
sits at the top of that service. New files are the last resort, not the default.

---

## Strict Architecture Boundaries (MANDATORY)

| Concern | Lives in | Never in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Request DTOs (classes + `class-validator` decorators) | `<module>/dto/<operation>.dto.ts` — one DTO per file; shared ones in `common/dto/` | controllers, services, `entities/` |
| Response shapes (interfaces/types — not validated, so not classes, per §5 rule 2) | `<module>/entities/*.ts`, or import the shared `QuoteDto` from `quotes` | inline in a controller/service signature |
| HTTP: routing, guards, param parsing, status codes | `*.controller.ts` | services |
| Business logic + Prisma queries | `*.service.ts` | controllers |
| The `PrismaClient` instance | `src/prisma/prisma.service.ts` only | anywhere else |

- **Controllers validate and delegate, nothing else.** The DTO + global `ValidationPipe` validate; the
  controller calls one service method and returns its result. No branching business rules, no Prisma calls,
  no response-envelope building in a controller.

  ```ts
  // ✅ RIGHT
  @Get(':slug/quotes')
  @UseGuards(OptionalJwtAuthGuard)
  findQuotes(@Param('slug') slug: string, @Query() query: SinQuotesQueryDto, @CurrentUser() user?: AuthUser) {
    return this.sinsService.findQuotesForSin(slug, query, user?.userId);
  }

  // ❌ WRONG — Prisma + ranking logic in the controller
  @Get(':slug/quotes')
  async findQuotes(@Param('slug') slug: string) {
    const sin = await this.prisma.sin.findUnique({ where: { slug } });
    return this.prisma.sinQuote.findMany({ where: { sinId: sin!.id }, orderBy: { relevanceScore: 'desc' } });
  }
  ```

- **Only `PrismaService` imports `PrismaClient`.** Every other file injects `PrismaService`
  (`constructor(private readonly prisma: PrismaService) {}`). Never `new PrismaClient()` in a service, script
  helper, or test. Importing *types and enums* from `@prisma/client` (`Prisma`, `QuoteType`, `HadithGrade`) is
  fine.
- Services never read `req.user`; they receive the typed user via `@CurrentUser()` from the controller (§7.2).
- Multi-row writes that must succeed together use `this.prisma.$transaction(...)`.
- Never return raw Prisma rows from a public endpoint when a DTO projection exists for that entity.

---

## Product-Safety Rules (CORRECTNESS GUARANTEES — not style preferences)

Breaking any of these is a product bug, even if every test passes and the code "looks fine".

1. **Grade policy gates every hadith.** `GradePolicy.assertRenderable(grade)` (from `modules/hadith/`, §4.3)
   must gate every code path that can return a `HADITH`-type quote. `MAWDU` (fabricated) is **never** served or
   selectable → `422 GRADE_NOT_PERMITTED`. `DAIF` and `UNGRADED` only when explicitly opted in
   (`includeWeak` / `grades`). Default is `SAHIH, HASAN`. Enforce in the DTO (`@NotMawdu()`) **and** re-assert
   in the service.
2. **The grade filter must not drop non-hadith rows.** Verses have `grade = NULL`; filter with
   `OR: [{ type: { not: QuoteType.HADITH } }, { grade: { in: allowedGrades } }]` (§4.1), never a bare
   `grade: { in: [...] }`. A unit test asserting a verse survives `grades=SAHIH` is mandatory.
3. **Links are upserted, never bare-created.** `SinQuote` / `GoodDeedQuote` writes go through
   `prisma.sinQuote.upsert` / `prisma.goodDeedQuote.upsert` keyed on the `@@unique` compound
   (`sinId_quoteId` / `goodDeedId_quoteId`) — never `create`, so a curator re-submitting updates the score
   instead of 500-ing on `P2002`. Both sides share one generic implementation in `ClassificationService` (§3.11).
4. **Ingestion never classifies.** `content-sync` may only write `Quote`, `Translation`, `SyncLog` and
   `Source.lastSyncedAt` (always `origin = API_CACHED`, upserted on `@@unique([apiProvider, externalId])`).
   It must **NEVER** write a `SinQuote`/`GoodDeedQuote` row — linking is the human curator's job through
   `classification` (ARCHITECTURE.md §2 "Ingestion is separate from classification"; TECHNICAL_PLAN D7;
   content-pipeline-plan §1). Re-syncing must never touch curation work.
5. **Cache, don't proxy.** User-facing requests read PostgreSQL only. No request handler calls Quran.com,
   Sunnah.com or any provider inline; providers are called only by `content-sync` runs.
6. **Arabic is the source of truth.** `textAr` is always returned. A translation is attached as
   `translation: { languageCode, text } | null` and never substitutes for the Arabic (§2.4).
7. **`rawPayload` is never serialised to a client** (§3.1). Neither is `passwordHash`, ever.
8. **Guest-first.** Endpoints #1–#18 require no token. Never add a guard to a public read "to be safe".

---

## API Conventions Are Fixed (do not reinvent per endpoint)

All defined in `backend-plan.md` §2 — implemented once, globally:

- Global prefix `/v1` (health excluded). A new version is a new controller folder, never a mutated `/v1` shape.
- Envelope: `{ data }` for a single resource, `{ data, meta }` for collections, applied by the global
  `ResponseEnvelopeInterceptor`. Paginated services return `{ data, meta }` built with the shared
  `PaginatedResult<T>` helper; others return the plain value and let the interceptor wrap it.
- Errors: only the `AllExceptionsFilter` shape `{ error: { code, message, details, path, method, requestId,
  timestamp } }` with stable `SCREAMING_SNAKE` codes and the Prisma→HTTP table in §2.5. Throw Nest
  `HttpException`s (`NotFoundException`, `ConflictException`, …) from services; never build an error body by
  hand. Never leak a Prisma message or stack in a `5xx`.
- Pagination: offset `page`/`limit`, `limit` max **100**, enforced in the DTO (reminder endpoints cap at 50, §5.3).
- Status codes per §2.6 (`201` + `Location` on create, `204` on delete, `409` duplicates, `422` invalid reference).
- IDs are UUIDs (`ParseUUIDPipe`); `Sin`, `GoodDeed`, `Tag` are addressed publicly by `slug`.
- `?lang=ar|en` via `LocaleQueryDto` on every read endpoint.

**A new endpoint that invents a different response shape, error shape, or pagination style is a bug.**

### DTO conventions (summary — full rules in §5)

One file per DTO named after the operation; `@IsOptional()` before the type validator; every string has
`@MaxLength`; arrays use `@TransformToArray()`; keep `forbidNonWhitelisted: true`. Until
`@nestjs/mapped-types` is installed (§10), write `Update*Dto` partials explicitly — don't pull in
`@nestjs/swagger` for `PartialType`.

---

## Auth Pattern Is Fixed

- Guards are opted into **per controller / per route** with `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)`,
  `@UseGuards(OptionalJwtAuthGuard)`, or `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)` + `@Roles('ADMIN')` for every
  `/admin` route (`RolesGuard` always after `JwtAuthGuard`). See `backend-plan.md` §7.2 and TECHNICAL_PLAN B5.
- **Do not register a global `APP_GUARD`** for auth unless the user confirms the plan changed.
- `OptionalJwtAuthGuard` must degrade a malformed/expired token to anonymous, never `401`, on endpoints 3, 7, 8, 9.
- Unknown email and wrong password return the identical `401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS`.

---

## Testing (MANDATORY — matches repo reality)

- **Vitest only.** Never add Jest, `ts-jest`, `@types/jest`, or `jest.config.*`. Use `vi.fn()` / `vi.mock()`;
  Vitest globals are on (`describe`, `it`, `expect` need no import).
- Unit specs sit **beside** the service: `src/modules/sins/sins.service.spec.ts`. Mock `PrismaService` through
  `Test.createTestingModule({ providers: [SinsService, { provide: PrismaService, useValue: prismaMock }] })`.
- E2E specs live in `test/*.e2e-spec.ts` (one per controller, §11.2), run against a real Postgres test
  database, never mocks. External providers are always stubbed with fixtures in `test/fixtures/<provider>/`.
- The must-have table in `backend-plan.md` §11.1 **is the checklist**: a module is not "done" until every case
  listed for it has a passing test. Copy those cases into the spec as `it(...)` names.
- Adding the `/v1` prefix breaks the scaffold's `test/app.e2e-spec.ts` — update/delete it in the same commit.

## Lint

**oxlint only** (`oxlint --type-aware src/ test/`). Never add `.eslintrc*`, `eslint.config.*`, or ESLint
packages to the backend. Prettier (`pnpm format`) is the formatter.

## Dependencies

Only add a package that appears in `backend-plan.md` §10 **for the phase being built**. Anything else — even a
"tiny helper" — requires asking the user first. Never re-add packages §10 lists as already present
(`@nestjs/config`, `@nestjs/axios`, `axios`, `class-validator`, `class-transformer`, `@prisma/client`, `prisma`,
`vitest`, `supertest`).

## Schema Changes Are Exceptional

`prisma/schema.prisma` is treated as **final**.

- The ONLY changes allowed without an explicit user request are the ones pre-approved in `backend-plan.md` §9:
  `User.passwordHash`, `User.role` + `enum UserRole`, `User.lastLoginAt` — shipped together in phase 4 as
  `prisma migrate dev --name add_user_auth_fields`.
- Any other model, field, index, or enum change requires asking the user first, and ships as its own
  `prisma migrate dev --name <description>` in its own commit — never silently bundled into a feature commit.
- Never edit an already-committed migration file. Never "fix" a query by changing the schema.

---

## Naming

- Booleans name the affirmative, current condition with `is`/`has`/`can`/`should`
  (`isExternalApi`, `hasNext`, `includeWeak`) — never `isNotFound`, `isReady` for "not loading".
- Service methods follow the plan's verbs: `findAll`, `findBySlug`, `findById`, `findQuotesFor*`, `link*`,
  `unlink*`. Don't rename a method the plan already names.
- Files are kebab-case (`grade-policy.ts`, `link-sin-quote.dto.ts`); classes PascalCase with a role suffix
  (`SinsService`, `LinkSinQuoteDto`, `RolesGuard`).
- Named constants for magic numbers/strings (`DEFAULT_ALLOWED_GRADES`, `VARIETY_SCORE_FLOOR`) — via
  `ConfigService` when environment-dependent.

## Error Handling & Logging

- Services throw Nest exceptions; the global filter formats them. Don't wrap every Prisma call in `try/catch`
  just to rethrow — catch only when translating a specific case (e.g. "unknown `quoteId`" → `422`).
- Use the injected Nest/pino logger, never `console.log`. Never log tokens, passwords or full `rawPayload`.

## Dead Code

Before finishing: delete unused exports, helpers, DTO fields, imports and commented-out code. No "for later"
stubs. Grep every new export — if nothing imports it, remove it.

---

## Scope Control (CRITICAL)

- ONLY touch files the task needs. Don't refactor unrelated modules, rename working code, or reformat files you
  didn't otherwise change.
- Changing a DTO field, a response shape, a status code, or an `error.code` is a **contract change** (the
  frontend mirrors these in `frontend/src/lib/types/api.ts`): flag it explicitly to the user, never slip it in.
- Don't add unrequested endpoints, features, query params, or config.
- If the task needs a change outside its scope, explain why and ask first.
- State assumptions explicitly; ask when the plan is silent on a decision instead of guessing.

## Pre-Finish / Pre-Push Checklist (MANDATORY)

Work through this explicitly; if a step doesn't apply, say so rather than silently skipping it. Commands are run
from the monorepo root (equivalent `pnpm <script>` inside `backend/`):

- [ ] `pnpm --filter backend exec prisma validate` passes — if `schema.prisma` was touched (it almost never
      should be; see "Schema Changes Are Exceptional").
- [ ] `pnpm --filter backend lint` passes (oxlint).
- [ ] `pnpm --filter backend test` passes, including the §11.1 cases for every touched module.
- [ ] Every new or changed endpoint has at least one e2e assertion (`pnpm --filter backend test:e2e`) covering
      the envelope shape and its main status code(s).
- [ ] All relative imports end in `.js`; no `require()`.
- [ ] No Prisma calls or business logic in controllers; nothing but `PrismaService` touches `PrismaClient`.
- [ ] Product-safety rules hold (grade policy, upsert links, no links written by `content-sync`, `rawPayload`
      never serialised).
- [ ] No `console.log`, no `debugger`, no commented-out code, no `any` / `as any`.
- [ ] No new dependency outside §10 without the user's approval.
- [ ] `git diff` reviewed end-to-end: every hunk maps to the task; no scope creep, no unrelated files.

## Git

- Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:` (optional scope, e.g.
  `feat(sins): add GET /v1/sins/:slug/quotes`). No ticket-ID requirement.
- Atomic commits: one logical change each. A schema migration is always its own commit.
- Never bypass hooks with `--no-verify`.
